            [
              ['The main process owns all side effects.', 'The renderer is sandboxed — contextIsolation, no Node, strict CSP — and is pure UI over typed IPC. Disk, network and subprocesses live in main.'],
              ['IPC is a typed contract.', 'Every channel is declared once, handled in the module matching its prefix, and mocked for the browser harness.'],
              ['Stores are projections.', 'Zustand stores mirror main-process state; the live title, tokens and context meter stay honest while a turn runs.'],
              ['Sessions are files.', 'pi writes a session when a turn ends; the sidebar is a scan of pi’s session directory. Phosphor appends bookmarks, jumps and forks to those files only while no pi owns them.'],
              ['Six extensions run inside pi.', 'artifacts, context-breakdown, headroom, mcp-status, tool-name-guard, worktree-paths — two of them can change or refuse what the model did.'],
              ['Failure is reported, not hidden.', 'Errors surface on the session’s chat; main-process detail goes to a rotating debug log with pi’s argv, stderr and exits.'],
            ].map(([h, p], i) => (
